Direct ACK static binding verifies exact Target resource, physical partition and prepared commitment (generation-2 Pulsar also artifact digest); Kafka Produce ACK is baseline-only, Pulsar ACK is baseline/dedup-only. An explicit EvidenceContext carries a pre-resolved provider-authentication snapshot responsible for full response correlation, sender/sequence and artifact authority. Missing/failed authentication retains the entry without first result/source advance. Transactional receipt, Journal/operator/absence branches remain disabled pending their Target recovery-domain verifier, not downgraded to direct ACK.

One accounted source batch writes PUBLISHED current Message/ref settlement, strict order successor, terminal history, payload retention only when no refs remain, Budget RESOLVED_AWAITING_FLOOR and SYSTEM/POSITION_SYSTEM first results/frontier. Execution charge is released only after authentication; commitment/allocated remain unchanged until the existing Floor protocol. Transfer mismatch is a durable STALE_SYSTEM_MUTATION rejection with unchanged Message/order/Budget. Shared accounting checks primary/mirror/total ownership; no manual quota decrement is introduced.

